hitecture stays resilient to cloud failures\"}],\"$undefined\"]}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5f:I[205411,[\"/_next/static/chunks/0-0o8zjuqab7b.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0-wyrs755k4-p.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0i.l9589uvx0j.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07n~9r3bo6_t_.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/05jguszscqe2t.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0bgb1-s946o7g.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/15lxb7jjl82fj.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/13twdpqxz8tr6.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0mbd~fobjqaya.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0t1wtc-7-~e~c.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07kiqkba00.os.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0ni~d5qt~j59u.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0g_miwgby_mg4.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\"],\"default\"]\n:HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/promoting-postgres-changes-safely-production/promoting-postgres-changes-1024x538-3188801a.jpg\",\"image\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"57:[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L5f\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/promoting-postgres-changes-safely-production/promoting-postgres-changes-1024x538-3188801a.jpg\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/promoting-postgres-changes-safely-production/promoting-postgres-changes-1024x538-3188801a.jpg\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Every developer has their own workflow for promoting database changes from development to production, but this becomes an especially tricky problem in certain applications – for example, \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://neon.com/use-cases/ai-agents\",\"children\":\"codegen platforms\"}],\". In platforms like \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://replit.com/\",\"children\":\"Replit\"}],\", each user may be building multiple versions of their app / running experiments in parallel while production environments can continue receiving writes while a new version is being built.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Applications that look like this (or essentially any system that maintains many Postgres environments at once, each reflecting different states) face similar challenges:\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"How do you test changes safely in isolation?\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"How do you promote schema and data to production without losing writes?\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"How do you refresh development with the latest production data?\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"How do you roll back instantly if something goes wrong?\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"And how do you do all of this without maintaining multiple disconnected databases or complex migration pipelines?\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Customers have asked us these questions many times at Neon: we support codegen platforms like \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://replit.com/\",\"children\":\"Replit\"}],\", CMS systems like \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://strapi.io/\",\"children\":\"Strapi\"}],\", and many other applications that need \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"a dev \u003c\u003e prod workflow that’s programmable, efficient, and fast to execute across hundreds or thousands of environments\"}],\". This blog post walks through a solution we’ve presented to these customers and ultimately implemented in production, so you can build your own setup without even talking to us.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Fun fact: I was a Solution Architect at Neon before moving to DevRel, so I can confidently say this workflow is true and tested.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"the-use-case-multiple-environments-diverging-data-and-schema\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"The Use Case: Multiple Environments, Diverging Data and Schema\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#the-use-case-multiple-environments-diverging-data-and-schema\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to The Use Case: Multiple Environments, Diverging Data and Schema\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeLinecap\":\"square\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"strokeWidth\":1.4,\"d\":\"m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75\"}]}]}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Let’s first take a look at the real workflows that pushed us to formalize this pattern. These examples come directly from customer conversations and they’re representative of a broad class of applications.\"}],\"\\n\",\"$L60\",\"\\n\",\"$L61\",\"\\n\",\"$L62\",\"\\n\",\"$L63\",\"\\n\",\"$L64\",\"\\n\",\"$L65\",\"\\n\",\"$L66\",\"\\n\",\"$L67\",\"\\n\",\"$L68\",\"\\n\",\"$L69\",\"\\n\",\"$L6a\",\"\\n\",\"$L6b\",\"\\n\",\"$L6c\",\"\\n\",\"$L6d\",\"\\n\",\"$L6e\",\"\\n\",\"$L6f\",\"\\n\",\"$L70\",\"\\n\",\"$L71\",\"\\n\",\"$L72\",\"\\n\",\"$L73\",\"\\n\",\"$L74\",\"\\n\",\"$L75\",\"\\n\",\"$L76\",\"\\n\",\"$L77\",\"\\n\",\"$L78\",\"\\n\",\"$L79\",\"\\n\",\"$L7a\",\"\\n\",\"$L7b\",\"\\n\",\"$L7c\",\"\\n\",\"$L7d\",\"\\n\",\"$L7e\",\"\\n\",\"$L7f\",\"\\n\",\"$L80\",\"\\n\",\"$L81\",\"\\n\",\"$L82\",\"\\n\",\"$L83\",\"\\n\",\"$L84\",\"\\n\",\"$L85\",\"\\n\",\"$L86\",\"\\n\",\"$L87\",\"\\n\",\"$L88\",\"\\n\",\"$L89\",\"\\n\",\"$L8a\",\"\\n\",\"$L8b\",\"\\n\",\"$L8c\",\"\\n\",\"$L8d\",\"\\n\",\"$L8e\",\"\\n\",\"$L8f\",\"\\n\",\"$L90\",\"\\n\",\"$L91\",\"\\n\",\"$L92\",\"\\n\",\"$L93\",\"\\n\",\"$L94\",\"\\n\",\"$L95\",\"\\n\",\"$L96\",\"\\n\",\"$L97\",\"\\n\",\"$L98\",\"\\n\",\"$L99\",\"\\n\",\"$L9a\",\"\\n\",\"$L9b\",\"\\n\",\"$L9c\",\"\\n\",\"$L9d\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,":HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/promoting-postgres-changes-safely-production/image-1024x162-488f3fd9.jpeg\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/promoting-postgres-changes-safely-production/image-1-1024x180-aa93f012.jpeg\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/promoting-postgres-changes-safely-production/image-2-1024x162-b494fb9b.jpeg\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/promoting-postgres-changes-safely-production/image-3-1024x162-6e9e4e93.jpeg\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/promoting-postgres-changes-safely-production/image-4-1024x162-db04d29b.jpeg\",\"image\"]\n60:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"promoting-from-preview-to-production-with-prod-writes-in-between\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Promoting from preview to production, with prod writes in between\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#promoting-from-preview-to-production-with-prod-writes-in-between\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Promoting from preview to production, with prod writes in between\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":\"$57:12:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n61:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"This fits a platform where customers edit content in preview environments before publishing. In the meantime, production isn’t static. It keeps receiving writes while a preview is open, such as form submissions or content edits from live users.\"}]\n62:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"The desired workflow looks like this:\"}]\n63:[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Create a preview environment to stage CMS or application changes\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Modify data and schema safely in that preview\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Publish those changes to production once they’re validated\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Ensure no production writes are lost in the process\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Avoid long waits (milliseconds to one second is fine, minutes are not)\"}],\"\\n\"]}]\n64:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"This is a classic scenario where traditional “migration-only” workflows break down. Production and preview can diverge, and manually merging database states would be very error-prone and operationally risky. This workflow is applied at scale, so there’s also additional concerns to think about:\"}]\n65:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Costs (how to maintain multiple long-lived environments efficiently)\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Stale previews (what happens when previews pile up or go unused)\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Endpoint behavior (is it necessary to switch endpoints or copy data on publish)\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Data safety (how to prevent or recover from data loss when promoting)\"}],\"\\n\"]}]\n66:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"promoting-from-preview-to-production-with-read-only-prod\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Promoting from preview to production, with read-only prod\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#promoting-from-preview-to-production-with-read-only-prod\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Promoting from preview to production, with read-only prod\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,",\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":\"$57:12:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n67:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"This scenario look similar vs the above, but with one key difference – production is read-only. All edits happen in previews, and only one preview will be chosen for publishing. The requirements:\"}]\n68:[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Ability to spin up many previews quickly\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"Promote \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"one\"}],\" preview to production cleanly\",[\"$\",\"br\",null,{}],\"Keep costs predictable with a potentially large number of previews\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Delete stale environments at any time without cleanup issues\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Publish changes without switching endpoints or rewriting application code\"}],\"\\n\"]}]\n69:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"The workflow described in this blog post serves both of these scenarios.\"}]}]\n6a:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"the-tool-for-the-job-neon-snapshots\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"The Tool for the Job: Neon Snapshots\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#the-tool-for-the-job-neon-snapshots\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to The Tool for the Job: Neon Snapshots\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":\"$57:12:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n6b:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"So, to recap the fundamental problem: when you have multiple environments that evolve independently, there is no safe way to “merge” two diverged database states. Code merges cleanly because files are text, databases do not. To circumvent this problem, our workflow is going to rely on \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://neon.com/blog/checkpoints-for-agents-with-neon-snapshots\",\"children\":\"Neon snapshots\"}],\", a feature built directly into Neon’s \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://neon.com/storage\",\"children\":\"storage architecture\"}],\".\"]}]\n6c:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"what-neon-snapshots-are\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading grou